{"name":"River Road","hex":"#ae8d6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"River Road","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Lane County, Oregon, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/River_Road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barbuda-South","blocks":[{"text":"Barbuda-South or Barbuda South River Road, is a village and enumeration district on the island of Barbuda."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbuda-South"},{"title":"River Road, Hamilton","blocks":[{"text":"River Road is a residential suburb of Hamilton, sited on the eastern bank of the Waikato River. The namesake road runs from Claudelands Bridge north to Pukete Bridge and beyond, to Ngāruawāhia, but the main part of the suburb is between Boundary Road and Donny Park. Properties close to the river are much more expensive than those further away. Most of River Road was shown on an 1865 map, though it was some years later before it was built and, by 1866, only one bridge had been built."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/RiverRdHouses.jpg/330px-RiverRdHouses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Road%2C_Hamilton"},{"title":"River Road (band)","blocks":[{"text":"River Road is an American country music band composed of Tony Ardoin, Mike Burch, Richard Comeaux, Steve Grisaffe, and Charles Ventre. Founded in 1989, the band signed to Capitol Records Nashville in 1997, releasing their self-titled debut album that year and charting three singles on the Billboard country charts, including the top 40 hit \"Nickajack\". By 1998, River Road had transferred to Virgin Records Nashville, charting a fourth single and recording an unreleased album. Ventre and Grisaffe each began solo careers in the 2000s, but they reunited with Ardoin and Burch in 2011 to release a new extended play."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Road_(band)"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Riverroadalbum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Riverroadalbum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARiverroadalbum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The major drainage basins in North America","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Perit